Location

Catherines Place occupies a wonderfully convenient location within approximately 0.7 mile of the High Street, known for its pretty, traditional feel with views towards the surrounding hills. There are a number of independent shops and restaurants all within a short distance. Of particular note is the recently redeveloped Tungsate Quarter with the Ivy Brasserie and Gail''s Bakery amongst its highlights. The area also features the historic Guildford Castle grounds, St Catherines Ruins, and country walks are varied including along the River Wey and the glorious North Downs, offering miles of footpaths and bridleways.

