Description

Occupying the entire top floor of the exclusive Albury Place on Epsom Road, this exceptional three bedroom, three bathroom penthouse offers sleek contemporary living in the heart of Guildford. Designed to maximise space and light, the property features a stunning open-plan kitchen with high end appliances, a spacious dining and living area and an abundance of natural light throughout.

The principal suite is complemented by two further generously sized bedrooms and beautifully appointed bathrooms, all finished to a high specification. A private roof terrace provides the perfect setting for entertaining or relaxing while enjoying elevated views across the surrounding area.

Further benefits include lift access to the penthouse level and the only two off-street parking spaces at the front of the building, offering both convenience and exclusivity.

Ideally positioned on sought-after Epsom Road, the property enjoys excellent access to Guildford’s highly regarded schools, a wide range of shops, restaurants and amenities, as well as superb transport connections including Guildford mainline station and nearby road links to London and the surrounding areas.

A rare opportunity to acquire a stylish and sophisticated penthouse in one of Guildford’s most desirable locations.

Location

Guildford High Street is known for its pretty, traditional feel with views towards the surrounding hills. There are a number of independent shops and restaurants all within a short distance. Tungsate Quarter is in close proximity, and boasts the Ivy Brasserie and Gail''s Bakery amongst its highlights. The area also features the historic Guildford Castle grounds and country walks are varied with Pewley Down and The Chantries close by.

There are two mainline stations in close proximity providing a choice of services into London with journey times from around 35 minutes. There are also fast services to Portsmouth and Gatwick airport. The main A3 provides a direct route to London and the south coast, linking at J10 with the M25 for the airports.

There are an excellent selection of state and private schools in the area including The Royal Grammar School, Tormead, George Abbott, Pewley Infant & Junior and Guildford High School.

Square Footage: 1,259 sq ft
Leasehold with approximately 117 years remaining.', 'Savills, Guildford', '2026-05-12T12:05:51Z', '2026-10-23T23:16:46Z', '["epc_current"]');

A lovely three bedroom family home set within a quiet residential cul-de-sac in Crofton Park, offering bright and well proportioned rooms, a private south facing garden, a garage and residents only parking. The property is offered to the market with no onward chain, making it an ideal option for many buyers, whether you are looking for a first purchase, or wishing to upsize for an additional bedroom or outside space.

Inside, the home provides a comfortable and practical layout. There are three bedrooms, including two generous doubles and a single that works well as a child’s room, home office or guest space. The family bathroom sits on the first floor, while the main bedroom benefits from its own en suite shower room. On the ground floor, the spacious lounge and dining area offers plenty of room for everyday living and entertaining, with good natural light throughout. The fitted kitchen requires modernisation, but presents an opportunity for buyers to add their own stamp on the proeprty, and the convenience of a downstairs WC adds to the overall functionality of the home.

The south facing garden is a real highlight, offering a sunny and private outdoor space that’s easy to enjoy throughout the year.

A further benefit is the garage, located closeby and offers additional storage, which is a rear bonus for a property in the local area.

The location is a key attraction. The home is ideally placed for local amenities and sits within easy reach of excellent transport links, popular schools and popular green spaces. Blythe Hill Fields, Hilly Fields and Ladywell Fields are all close by, offering wide open spaces, play areas and walking routes that are perfect for families and those who enjoy time outdoors.', 'Bryan & Keegan, London', '2026-05-12T16:58:07Z', '2026-10-23T23:09:17Z', '["floor_level"]');

INSIDE

Entered on the fifth floor, the apartment opens into a striking open-plan living, dining and kitchen space arranged around expansive triple glazing and direct access to a private balcony with panoramic London views. Oak flooring with underfloor heating runs throughout, while distinct living and dining zones create a layout equally suited to everyday living and entertaining.

The kitchen is sleek and architectural in feel, centred around matte airbrushed cabinetry and fully integrated Smeg appliances. Further thoughtful additions include a reverse osmosis drinking water system and a whole-home soft water system connected to all outlets and appliances. A generous guest WC and separate utility cupboard complete this level.

A sculptural balustraded staircase leads down to the bedroom floor, where custom Luxaflex thermal blackout blinds and natural fibre carpets introduce a softer, quieter material palette. The principal suite is particularly impressive, featuring a bespoke LEMMA Italian walk-in wardrobe and a luxurious en-suite bathroom with double shower and separate full-sized bath.

The second bedroom is also an excellent double, extending to approximately 167 sq ft, with its own en-suite shower room and access to a substantial under-stairs storage cupboard.

The building has a concierge, secure entry system, as well as a beautifully maintained communal garden, bicycle storage for residents and an exercise room.

NEIGHBOURHOOD & CONNECTIONS

At the heart of Hackney Downs is the park itself — directly overlooked by The Otto Building. A large and well-kept green space, it offers tennis courts, a basketball court, children’s playground, and wide open lawns — perfect for sports, dog walking, and picnics.

Hackney Downs Station is the area’s key rail hub, offering fast and regular London Overground services to Liverpool Street in around ten minutes — ideal for commuters and city workers. Hackney Central Station is also within walking distance, expanding connectivity via the Overground to Stratford, Highbury & Islington, and westwards towards Shepherd’s Bush. Numerous bus routes and cycle lanes weave through the borough, ensuring effortless travel across East and Central London.

Close by, Hackney Downs Studios provides a creative hub of independent businesses, artist studios, cafés, and event spaces — perfect for coffee, workshops, and supporting local makers.

For dining, locals love Casa Fofo, a Michelin-starred fine dining spot, and Uchi Bake, a Japanese bakery and sushi restaurant that has fast become a neighbourhood favourite.', 'Scotts, London', '2026-05-14T16:53:26Z', '2026-10-23T22:53:35Z', '["floor_level"]');
Offered to the market in the highly regarded and sought after Fairway Avenue located just off Halls Road is this spacious and well-presented four-bedroom detached family home sitting in an enviable position overlooking Calcot Park Golf Course. Set within a generous sized plot, the property is an ideal home for a large family or someone who enjoys entertaining due to the ample accommodation and outside space. Set over two floors and significantly extended in 2014, this Cooks built home offers versatile living accommodation and benefits from three reception rooms, conservatory, as well as a generous re-fitted kitchen/dining/living room, utility room and a W.C. Upstairs there are four well-proportioned bedrooms with the primary suite benefitting from a 3 double wardrobes, en-suite shower room and stunning views of the garden. A stylish 4 piece family bathroom. There is an In and Out driveway and a beautiful mature garden at the rear. EPC Rating C.

Local Information
Tilehurst, and Tilehurst Village is located in the western suburbs of Reading, is a vibrant residential area with convenient access to urban amenities. The area features a mix of historic homes and modern developments, surrounded by green spaces such as Prospect Park and Arthur Newbery Park. Tilehurst offers a large range of local shops, schools, and community facilities, making it popular with families. It has excellent transport links, being very close to J12 of the M4 and there is also Tilehurst station which is just two stops from Reading station providing easy access to London Paddington and beyond.

