Set within a handsome Grade II Listed Georgian end of terrace building, the recently refurbished communal areas provide an elegant welcome. Internally, the flat comprises a bright reception room with two sash windows overlooking Canonbury Square, a spacious kitchen diner with views over the communal garden, a well appointed bathroom, and two well proportioned double bedrooms. The principal bedroom is positioned to the front of the property, while the second bedroom enjoys a peaceful rear aspect.

The property is perfectly positioned to enjoy the area''s exceptional selection of independent amenities. On your doorstep are renowned local favourites including The Compton Arms, Canonbury Tavern, The Marquess Tavern,
Trullo and Prawn on the Lawn to name just a few, while nearby Upper Street offers an extensive array of boutique shops, delicatessens, cafés, bars and restaurants.

For those who enjoy green spaces, both Highbury Fields and the New River Path are just moments away. Canonbury Square itself provides a beautiful, verdant oasis, with mature trees creating a stunning natural canopy throughout the year.

Transport connections are excellent with Highbury & Islington Station, providing access to the Victoria line and London Overground services, is just a short walk away. Angel Underground Station (Northern line) and Essex Road Station, with direct services to Moorgate, are also within easy walking distance. Combining an enviable location with attractive surroundings and excellent connectivity, this superb home offers the very best of both Canonbury and Islington.', 'NEILSON & BAUER LTD, Islington', '2026-07-09T14:18:10Z', '2026-10-23T22:52:13Z', '["floor_level"]');
The ground floor offers a particularly flexible layout, with a spacious kitchen/diner providing an excellent hub for family life and entertaining, alongside a separate lounge and sitting room. There is also a further kitchen/dining and living area within the annexe accommodation, together with a shower room, utility room and workshop/store, making the property exceptionally versatile for a large or extended family, those working from home or anyone requiring separate living space.
Upstairs, the main house provides well-proportioned bedrooms including a generous principal bedroom with dressing room and en-suite bathroom, together with two further bedrooms and a family bathroom. The overall accommodation is complemented by the additional space available within the loft, giving the property an unusually high degree of flexibility. The loft is already prepared with first-fix plumbing, electrics and heating in place, meaning the essential services are ready to go. The space simply requires finishing by the new owners and offers the opportunity to create an additional bedroom, home office, hobby room, games room, extensive storage or bathroom, subject to any necessary consents.
To the front, the property benefits from a truly impressive, fully paved driveway providing extensive off-road parking for multiple vehicles. The driveway is enclosed by a controlled electric gate, offering an added level of security, privacy and convenience while also creating an attractive approach to the house.
The rear garden is equally impressive, providing a wonderful private outdoor space with a combination of paved patio areas, seating spaces, established greenery and a charming pond. There is plenty of room for outdoor dining, entertaining and relaxing, while the established planting gives the garden a mature and secluded feel.
At the far end of the garden is a separate studio which is in immaculate condition and provides an excellent additional space away from the main house. As shown on the floorplan, the studio comprises a generous main room, kitchenette and en-suite shower room, making it ideal as a home office, gym, creative space, guest accommodation or independent workspace. Its position within the garden provides excellent separation from the main property and makes it particularly useful for modern family life.
The property also benefits from a location that combines the convenience of Tilehurst and Reading with easy access to surrounding countryside. There are a good range of local schools, shops and everyday amenities nearby, while Tilehurst offers regular transport links into Reading and connections beyond. The number 17 bus route is approximately 100 metres from the property and runs throughout the night, providing a direct link to Reading Station. This makes a convenient door-to-door journey to London Paddington possible in approximately 35 minutes, offering an excellent option for commuters. Tilehurst railway station also provides services towards Reading, London Paddington and Oxford, while the nearby M4 provides convenient road connections towards London, the wider Thames Valley and the West Country.
Overall, this is a substantial and highly adaptable detached family home offering excellent existing accommodation, exceptional parking, a generous private garden, an immaculate detached studio and a loft that is already equipped with first-fix plumbing, electrics and heating, ready for completion by the new owners. With its combination of space, versatility, privacy, transport links and location, this is a property that needs to be viewed to fully appreciate everything it has to offer.', 'Arins Property Services, Tilehurst', '2026-07-09T17:09:34Z', '2026-10-23T23:14:08Z', '[]');
