Quietly situated in the Medway conservation area, this split-level apartment sits within the former gymnasium of a converted 19th-century school. The result is one of tremendous scale, with ceilings almost 5m high, a generous mezzanine level, and large south-facing sash windows. Mile End station is a short walk south, and Victoria Park’s lush open spaces are just to the north.

The Tour

The building presents an imposing silhouette with an enormous sense of scale and volume – characteristics echoed within the apartment. A bicycle store occupies the building’s ground floor, and the apartment is accessed on the first floor.

Upon entering, the interiors immediately display strong character; the gymnasium’s original herringbone parquet flooring runs beneath and filtered light edges in from the living space beyond. The entrance hall provides coat storage.

The wonderfully bright living room feels incredibly spacious, thanks to a double-height ceiling, with bespoke wall shelving (both practical and decorative) and a large south-facing sash window that brings in light from dawn till dusk. The plan makes excellent use of the space, with a generous mezzanine that leverages the sense of scale and storage beneath the stairs.

The kitchen and bedroom are situated on the mezzanine, each decently sized and subtly delineated by a curtain rail. Accessed from the hall, the bathroom features a shower over the bath and additional storage cupboards.

The Area

Positioned along a tree-lined residential street, Schoolbell Mews is ideally located just moments from the popular amenities, independent shops, and bustling weekend markets of Roman Road. For green space, the expansive open grounds and historic charm of Victoria Park lie just to the north.

Transport links are exceptionally convenient, with Mile End station, offering quick access across the capital via the Central, District, and Hammersmith & City lines, within a short walk to the south.

