The neighbourhood is full of character. Nearby is The Widow’s Son, a charming local pub famous for its centuries-old tradition of adding a hot cross bun to its collection every Good Friday. The Angel of Bow is also close by. For coffee and brunch, Les Miches and the café at Poplar Union are local favourites. Everyday shops and services are all within easy reach, and Bow itself has some of East London’s best pubs.

Victoria Park is also close by. Often called the “People’s Park”, it offers lakes, open green spaces, cafés and sports facilities, all on your doorstep. It’s hugely popular with joggers and cyclists, who make the most of its wide, tree-lined paths and the canal towpaths that connect to it. Families love its playgrounds and boating lake, and dog walkers gather throughout the day, giving it a wonderfully friendly, community feel. At weekends the park really comes alive with its incredible markets, where you’ll find street food from around the world, freshly baked bread, artisan coffee, local produce and handmade goods. It’s the perfect way to spend a relaxed weekend morning.', 'Huttons & Partners, London', '2026-10-23T18:17:03Z', '2026-10-23T23:02:16Z', '["floor_level"]');

